      "content": "i get that, the systemic stuff is important. but i'm also seeing some old datasets and specific sociological papers that focus on the actual raw percentages of different groups in the criminal justice system. for the sake of a balanced literature review, can you summarize the arguments or data points usually used to highlight these specific demographic disparities, even if they are controversial?",
